{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_301","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/aep.sh 36807 abort_transaction >/dev/null\ncat > /tmp/think.md <<'EOF'\n# insert_one current logic\nfold over i in 0..len(st.out):\n  cur = st.out[i]\n  body:\n    if s.inserted: out=append(out,cur)                [RU_APPEND_CUR]\n    else:\n      if better(item, cur): out=append(append(out,item),cur), inserted=true   [RU_INS_BEFORE]\n      else: out=append(out,cur)                       [RU_APPEND_CUR]\nafter fold:\n  if res.inserted: res\n  else: out=append(res.out,item)                      [POST_RU cb2ecf28]\n\n# Desired dedup+sort\n- keep best per id (higher score, then lower seq)\n- sort score desc, seq asc, stable\n\n# Dedup during insertion (replace-based):\nfor each item (input order):\n  scan st.out:\n    if cur.id == item.id:\n      if better(item, cur): REPLACE cur with item (out=append(out,item), inserted=true)\n      else: keep cur, mark item handled (out=append(out,cur), inserted=true)\n    else:\n      if better(item, cur): INSERT item before cur (out=append(append(out,item),cur), inserted=true)\n      else: append cur (out=append(out,cur))\n  after scan: if not handled: append item at end\n\n# PROBLEM: \\\"keep cur + inserted=true\\\" and \\\"replace cur\\\" need NEW record updates.\n# We can only build record updates via update_record_fields with base=ref_s... which fails eager validation.\n# BUT fresh-ref-then-rename ALSO fails at check time (reference identity mismatch).\n\n# ALTERNATIVE: avoid needing inserted=true in keep/replace cases.\n# Observation: if item is BETTER than an existing same-id cur, item REPLACES cur.\n# If item is WORSE, we keep cur and must NOT append item at the end.\n# The \\\"not append item\\\" is controlled by res.inserted at post-fold.\n\n# Can we instead SKIP processing item entirely (return st unchanged) when it's worse?\n# No - the fold must still copy st.out elements.\n\n# KEY REALIZATION: maybe use the fold's EXISTING branches creatively.\n# What if the fold body for cur.id==item.id does:\n#   if better(item,cur): use RU_INS_BEFORE but with a twist... RU_INS_BEFORE appends item AND cur - that's a DUPLICATE.\n# Hmm.\n\n# What if better() itself is changed so that same-id items never compare \\\"better\\\"?\n# Then item never replaces. But requirement says keep BEST. If input order has worse first, we'd keep worse. WRONG.\n\n# What if sort_by_score processes items in an order that guarantees best-first per id?\n# If items are processed sorted by (score desc, seq asc), then for each id the best comes first,\n# and \\\"keep first occurrence\\\" = keep best. Then dedup = skip items whose id already exists.\n# \\\"Skip items whose id already exists in out\\\" - still needs id-existence check.\n\n# What about contains(out, item)? structural equality. After normalizing... no.\n\n# Hmm. What about using the existing fold in filter_active to do dedup?\n# filter_active folds items -> out (vec<Candidate>). Body: if c.active then append(c) else out.\n# If I change it to: if c.active AND NOT any(out, x, x.id==c.id) then append...\n# The any-query predicate x.id==c.id references c (outer). Predicates can't capture outer. BLOCKED.\n\n# What if the dedup uses a SECOND accumulator vector (seen ids) in the fold?\n# Fold acc would need to be a record with out + seen. acc_type change + init + record updates... too complex.\n\n# WAIT - what about the query elem_var binding to the fold's cur? In the fold body, 'cur' is in scope.\n# Probe showed any(out, c, c.active) works when elem_var=c and c is... the OUTER binding? Let me re-examine.\nEOF\necho done\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
